prompts.template:
Write a {{length}} {{genre}} story.

Setting: {{setting}}
Main character: {{protagonist}}
Central conflict: {{conflict}}
Tone: {{tone}}

Include:
- A strong opening that hooks the reader
- Vivid sensory details
- Dialogue that reveals character
- A satisfying {{endingType}} ending

Write in {{perspective}} perspective.

Generate {{count}} headline options for the following content.

Topic: {{topic}}
Audience: {{audience}}
Tone: {{tone}}
Style mix: {{styleMix}}

For each headline:
- Keep it under {{maxWords}} words
- Make it specific and benefit-driven
- Vary the approach (question, how-to, listicle, bold claim, curiosity gap)

Number each headline and add a one-line note on why it works.

Write a product description for {{productName}}.

Product type: {{productType}}
Key features: {{features}}
Target buyer: {{buyer}}
Tone: {{tone}}

Structure:
1. Attention-grabbing opening (benefit-first, not feature-first)
2. 3-4 bullet points highlighting key features
3. Short paragraph on how it fits the buyer's life
4. One line addressing a common objection: {{objection}}

Keep total length under {{wordLimit}} words.

Write a {{duration}}-minute speech for {{occasion}}.

Speaker: {{speakerRole}}
Audience: {{audience}}
Main message: {{mainMessage}}
Tone: {{tone}}

Include:
1. Opening hook (story, question, or bold statement)
2. {{sectionCount}} main points with transitions
3. One memorable quote or statistic
4. Call-to-action or closing thought
5. [Speaker notes] for pacing and emphasis

Format: Write as spoken words, not essay prose. Use short sentences.

You are an expert marketing strategist and copywriter.

Create an influencer campaign brief for {{brand}}.

Campaign: {{campaignName}}
Product/service: {{product}}
Target creator type: {{creatorType}}
Platform: {{platform}}

Include:
1. Campaign overview and goals
2. Key messages ({{messageCount}} must-include points)
3. Content deliverables: {{deliverables}}
4. Do's and Don'ts for brand representation
5. Hashtags and tags to use: {{tags}}
6. Timeline and posting schedule
7. Compensation structure: {{compensation}}
8. Approval process

Tone for creators: {{tone}}

Output format:
- Use clear headings and numbered sections
- Be specific and actionable — no filler or generic advice
- If something is unknown, state a reasonable assumption in brackets

Quality checklist before you finish:
- Every section requested is included
- Copy is ready to use (not placeholder lorem ipsum)
- Tone matches the brief throughout

You are an expert marketing and positioning strategist.

Customize the following generic task for this specific market:

Generic task: {{genericTask}}

Industry: {{industry}}
Product type: {{productType}}
Niche / audience: {{niche}}
Brand name: {{brandName}}
Unique angle: {{uniqueAngle}}
Tone: {{tone}}

Rewrite the task as a complete, copy-paste ready AI prompt that:
1. Uses industry-specific vocabulary (not generic marketing speak)
2. References pain points and buying triggers for {{niche}}
3. Includes constraints that matter in {{industry}} (compliance, seasonality, local context, etc.)
4. Specifies output format suited to {{productType}} businesses
5. Adds 3 example phrases or hooks that would resonate with this niche
6. Notes what to avoid (clichés, wrong tone, off-brand claims)

Output format:
- Use clear headings and numbered sections
- Be specific and actionable — no filler or generic advice
- If something is unknown, state a reasonable assumption in brackets

You are an expert local restaurant marketer.

Create a {{weekCount}}-week social content pack for {{restaurantName}}.

Cuisine: {{cuisine}}
Location: {{location}}
Vibe: {{vibe}}
Signature dish: {{signatureDish}}
Goal: {{goal}}
Platforms: {{platforms}}

For each week provide:
- 3 Instagram captions (with emoji, local hashtags, CTA to book/visit)
- 1 Google Business post (under 150 words, with offer or event angle)
- 1 story idea (photo/video concept, not just text)

Include:
- Local SEO keywords naturally (neighborhood name, cuisine + city)
- Seasonal or weekly special angle
- User-generated content prompt (ask customers to post X)
- Do NOT use generic food puns or "foodie heaven" clichés

Tone: {{tone}}

Output format:
- Use clear headings by week
- Be specific and actionable — ready to post

You are an expert e-commerce copywriter.

Write a product listing for {{productName}} on {{platform}}.

Product: {{productDescription}}
Target buyer: {{targetBuyer}}
Price point: {{pricePoint}}
Top 3 benefits: {{benefits}}
Keywords to include: {{keywords}}

Deliver:
1. Product title (max {{titleLimit}} characters, front-load main keyword)
2. {{bulletCount}} bullet points (benefit-led, not feature-dump)
3. Product description ({{descLength}}) — story + specs + social proof placeholder
4. A+ content module ideas (3 comparison or lifestyle blocks)
5. Backend search terms / tags (if applicable)
6. 3 subject lines for abandoned-cart email featuring this product

Avoid: superlatives without proof, keyword stuffing, duplicate bullets.
Tone: {{tone}}

You are an expert real estate copywriter.

Write listing copy for {{propertyAddress}}.

Property type: {{propertyType}}
Bed/bath/sqft: {{specs}}
Standout features: {{features}}
Neighborhood selling points: {{neighborhood}}
Price range: {{priceRange}}
Target buyer: {{targetBuyer}}

Deliver:
1. MLS description ({{mlsLength}}, factual but evocative — no fair housing violations)
2. Instagram/Facebook teaser (hook + 3 bullets + CTA for showing)
3. Open house invitation email
4. 5 headline options for Zillow/Realtor.com
5. Agent talking points for showings (what to highlight in each room)

Compliance: No references to family status, religion, race, or disability. Describe the property and neighborhood amenities only.
Tone: {{tone}}

You are an expert fitness content strategist.

Create a {{weekCount}}-week content plan for {{coachName}}, a {{specialty}} coach.

Target client: {{targetClient}}
Transformation promise: {{transformation}}
Offer: {{offer}}
Platforms: {{platforms}}

Each week include:
- 2 Reel/TikTok scripts (hook in first 2 seconds, {{reelLength}} max)
- 2 carousel post outlines (slide-by-slide)
- 1 engagement question for stories
- 1 lead magnet idea tied to {{offer}}

Avoid: before/after body shaming, unrealistic timelines, medical claims without disclaimer.
Tone: {{tone}}
Include disclaimer line for health content where needed.

You are an expert course launch strategist.

Build a sales funnel for {{courseName}}.

Topic: {{courseTopic}}
Target student: {{targetStudent}}
Transformation: {{transformation}}
Price: {{price}}
Launch model: {{launchModel}}

Deliver:
1. Sales page outline (headline, pain, promise, curriculum, testimonials placeholder, CTA, guarantee)
2. {{emailCount}}-email pre-launch sequence (value-first, pitch in email 4+)
3. Webinar/workshop script outline (45 min: hook, teaching, offer, Q&A)
4. 5 objection handlers (price, time, "will it work for me", etc.)
5. Urgency element that isn't fake scarcity

Tone: {{tone}}

You are an expert agency new-business strategist.

Create a pitch for {{agencyName}} pursuing {{prospectName}}.

Agency specialty: {{agencySpecialty}}
Prospect industry: {{prospectIndustry}}
Prospect pain: {{prospectPain}}
Proposed scope: {{proposedScope}}
Budget range: {{budgetRange}}

Deliver:
1. Cover email (under 200 words — insight-led, not "we're great")
2. Deck outline ({{slideCount}} slides: situation, insight, approach, proof, team, investment, next steps)
3. One relevant case study angle (even if anonymized)
4. 3 discovery questions to ask before the pitch meeting
5. Objection prep: "You're too small / too expensive / we have an agency"

Tone: {{tone}}

You are an expert D2C brand storyteller.

Write brand story and About page copy for {{brandName}}.

Product: {{product}}
Founder origin: {{founderOrigin}}
Mission: {{mission}}
Values: {{values}}
What makes you different: {{differentiator}}
Target customer: {{targetCustomer}}

Deliver:
1. One-sentence brand mission
2. About page ({{pageLength}}) — founder story arc: problem → journey → solution → today
3. "Why we exist" manifesto (short, punchy paragraph)
4. 3 customer-facing value props (not features)
5. Instagram bio + pinned post caption introducing the brand
